<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Jabani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1500</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Jabani was fought in 1500 in Shirvan, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>, between the young Safavid leader Ismail and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shirvanshah">Shirvanshah</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/farrukh-yasar">Farrukh Yasar</a>. Ismail's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qizilbash">Qizilbash</a> won, and Farrukh Yasar was killed, avenging the deaths of Ismail's father and grandfather at the hands of the Shirvanshahs. The victory opened the way for Ismail's capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a> in 1501 and the founding of the Safavid state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-jabani.jpg" alt="Battle of Jabani" width="320" height="416" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artistUnknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1541-Battle_in_the_war_between_Shah_Isma%27il_and_the_King_of_Shirvan-Shahnama-i-Isma%27il.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
